        "id": "i",
        "text": "How should he read them before any calculation?",
        "marks": 1,
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "$3p$ means $3 \\times p$, and $9(z+5)$ means $9$ times the whole of $(z+5)$."
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "$3p$ names an omitted multiplication sign as a new letter, not three times $p$."
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "The value is whichever numeral appears first in the writing."
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "text": "$3p$ still means multiplication even if the letter stands alone with no numeral beside it."
          }
        ]
      },
